&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Basics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are&amp;nbsp;seeking&amp;nbsp;a skilled and experienced Business Analyst proficient in Salesforce Sales&amp;nbsp;Cloud. This role will have their hands in a little bit of everything but will specialize in gathering and&amp;nbsp;maintaining&amp;nbsp;requirements for our portfolio of projects,&amp;nbsp;assist&amp;nbsp;with functional and technical design, test and evaluate new and existing technologies during concept validations. This person will also act as a liaison between stakeholders in our Sales, Partner, Marketing, Commercial Ops, and Finance organizations and work as a member of the Business Systems team to ensure transparency and&amp;nbsp;timely&amp;nbsp;delivery of project deliverables. The ideal candidate will play a pivotal role in&amp;nbsp;optimizing our use of Salesforce to enhance customer experience, streamline processes, and drive business growth. The role requires a deep understanding of Salesforce overall functionalities, coupled with the ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position follows the Company’s hybrid schedule which currently requires employees to work in the office at one of the following locations a minimum of&amp;nbsp;three days per week: Addison, TX; Bellevue, WA; Durham, NC; Emeryville, CA; or Reston, VA.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works collaboratively with other members of the Sales Systems team to ensure the requirements are understood and documented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with stakeholders to shape requirements and ensure alignment with business/technology strategy and planned initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist&amp;nbsp;in the planning, prioritization, design,&amp;nbsp;development&amp;nbsp;and deployment of new projects &amp;amp; system enhancements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for understanding business requirements, creating/grooming user stories, and partnering with the delivery team to deliver solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage business knowledge and&amp;nbsp;expertise&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;opportunities for process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and perform system testing to ensure requirements are met. Work closely with the project team during user acceptance testing (UAT); including tracking issues through to resolution and securing end user acceptance sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business operations team members to define, plan, and execute small and medium projects, in addition to ongoing delivery of ‘run the business’ enhancements and fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in Computer Science, MIS, Computer&amp;nbsp;Engineering&amp;nbsp;or similar technical degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Sales Cloud Consultant and Salesforce Administrator Certifications strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce CPQ Specialist Certification or Business Analyst Certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a business analyst/implementation consultant/solutions architect supporting Salesforce platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with declarative development on the Salesforce platform as an administrator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and supporting small to medium scale, complex solutions on Salesforce and associated ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of software testing with knowledge on building test plans and executing them in unit, functional and user acceptance test cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to excel in a fast growing/fast paced environment delivering accuracy where adaptability is imperative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Agile/Scrum methodologies is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated understanding of Change Management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance multiple tasks simultaneously; workload will be a blend of small, medium, and large projects as well as ongoing production support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
