&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this full-time position is $135,000 to $210,000. This range is an estimate for what Tanium will pay a new hire. The actual annual base salary offered may be adjusted based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, location, education, skills, training, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to an annual base salary, team members will receive equity awards and a generous benefits package consisting of medical, dental and vision plan, family planning benefits, health savings account, flexible spending account, transportation savings account, 401(k) retirement savings plan with company match, life, accident and disability coverage, business travel accident insurance, employee assistance programs, disability insurance, and other well-being benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tanium is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, protected Veteran status, or other legally protected categories. If you require a reasonable accommodation in searching for a job opening, completing an application, interviewing, or completing any pre-employment testing or requirements, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@tanium.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@tanium.com&lt;/a&gt;. For more information refer to the “Know Your Rights” poster which is available here -&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/poster&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.eeoc.gov/poster&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be aware of job offers coming from people claiming to be Tanium employees. Tanium employees will only use @tanium.com email addresses to communicate with you, will have video interviews with you, and will never ask you for money.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cigna.com/legal/compliance/machine-readable-files&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;This link&lt;/a&gt; leads to the machine readable files that are made available in response to the federal Transparency in Coverage Rule and includes negotiated service rates and out-of-network allowed amounts between health plans and healthcare providers. The machine-readable files are formatted to allow researchers, regulators, and application developers to more easily access and analyze data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:1440,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;For more information on how Tanium processes your personal data, please see our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tanium.com/privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-auth=&quot;NotApplicable&quot; data-safelink=&quot;true&quot; data-linkindex=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is hybrid with 3 days in the office weekly (Cracow, Fabryczna)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Basics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tanium QA Engineers test products built on the Tanium platform, working with developers and product managers to construct and execute test plans, build automation frameworks, and file detailed bug reports that keep quality high across every release.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong technical skills are essential. If you are not comfortable hunting down resource leaks while simulating hundreds of thousands of clients, scripting environment configuration for dozens of target OS&#39;s, or building automation for a complex distributed platform — this may not be the place for you. If these things sound as exciting to you as they do to us, then Tanium could be your new home!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain automated test suites across UI, API, and integration layers using Python/pytest, Playwright, and REST API testing tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a shift-left, automation-first approach — embed in engineering squads, write in-sprint automation, and ensure test coverage keeps pace with feature development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain automated regression pipelines in CI/CD environments — monitoring pipeline health, resolving flaky tests, and ensuring reliable signal to engineering teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and execute test plans and test cases covering functional, regression, integration, performance, and basic security testing scenarios&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, document, and track defects using established defect management procedures — providing clear, reproducible bug reports and validating fixes with engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with software engineers and product managers throughout the development lifecycle — participating in design reviews, sprint planning, and code reviews to surface quality risks early&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain QA documentation including test plans, test summary reports, and deployment checklists aligned with the team&#39;s QA strategy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge and best practices within the Krakow QA team, contributing to a culture of continuous quality improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education&lt;br&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Computer Science, IT or other relevant degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of QA engineering experience with a strong focus on test automation in a B2B software or SaaS environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python/Pytest for automation, or experience with any other programming languages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with REST API testing and integrating automated tests into CI/CD pipelines (Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or GitLab CI)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of testing best practices including the test automation pyramid, Page Object Model, Agile/Scrum development, and defect management tools (Jira, TestRail)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with non-functional testing (load, stress, performance) and basic security testing concepts (OWASP); ISTQB CTFL certification preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal English communication skills — able to write clear bug reports and collaborate effectively with global engineering teams&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have experience
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Playwright or Selenium for UI testing; familiarity with TypeScript or JavaScript is a plus &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of operating systems (Linux &amp;amp; Windows preferred); how they are installed and configured &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with virtualization - VMware, Hyper-V, UTM, and similar&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with scripting languages - shell, Python, PowerShell, etc., and familiar with their use for streamlining day to day tasks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in using packet capture tools (Wireshark, tcpdump, etc) &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Additional offering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive remuneration and comprehensive benefits &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All full-time employees are eligible to receive restricted stock units. You can own part of the company you help to build&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A value-based, transparent culture that fosters collaboration and innovation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on complex and strategic global projects and initiatives &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career development opportunities &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, vision and basic dental coverage - Tanium paying 100% of the premium&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Disability + Critical Illness benefits - Tanium paying 100% of the premium&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free food in the office (via Wolt application)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multisport &amp;amp; MyBenefit platform&lt;/li&gt;
